From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 11:01:37 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] bonito: sepolicy for two HALs Android 17 started denying

The health HAL reads /sys/class/typec to get charger and port state.
Android 17 labels that directory sysfs_typec, a type introduced at board
API 202604, and no vendor rule grants it, so the HAL is denied on every
poll -- 150 denials in one boot, 54 in the next. Basic charging still
works (the battery reports USB powered and a correct level), so what is
lost is port and accessory detail rather than charging itself.

The gadget HAL reads vendor.usb.config to find the configured function
list. hal_usb_impl has set_prop for that type and nothing ever had
get_prop, so the read is denied.

Not fixed here, deliberately: sensors.qti is denied read/write on
/dev/diag, and granting a sensor daemon the Qualcomm diag interface is a
bigger concession than the one denial per boot is worth. The nfc app
domain is denied search on nfc_vendor_data_file, which is a core domain
and wants its rule placed with more care than a vendor .te.
---
 sepolicy/vendor/google/hal_health_default.te  | 4 ++++
 sepolicy/vendor/google/hal_usb_gadget_impl.te | 3 +++
 2 files changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sepolicy/vendor/google/hal_health_default.te b/sepolicy/vendor/google/hal_health_default.te
index 8d4613f5..2aeb0120 100644
--- a/sepolicy/vendor/google/hal_health_default.te
+++ b/sepolicy/vendor/google/hal_health_default.te
@@ -25,3 +25,7 @@ set_prop(hal_health_default, vendor_battery_defender_prop)
 
 allow hal_health_default self:capability2 wake_alarm;
 allow hal_health_default mnt_vendor_file:dir search;
+
+# Android 17 labels /sys/class/typec sysfs_typec, a type new at board API 202604, and the health
+# HAL walks the port to read charger state. Without this it is denied on every poll.
+r_dir_file(hal_health_default, sysfs_typec)
diff --git a/sepolicy/vendor/google/hal_usb_gadget_impl.te b/sepolicy/vendor/google/hal_usb_gadget_impl.te
index ddd90c2f..0a166848 100644
--- a/sepolicy/vendor/google/hal_usb_gadget_impl.te
+++ b/sepolicy/vendor/google/hal_usb_gadget_impl.te
@@ -12,3 +12,6 @@ set_prop(hal_usb_gadget_impl, vendor_usb_prop)
 allow hal_usb_gadget_impl sysfs_batteryinfo:dir r_dir_perms;
 allow hal_usb_gadget_impl sysfs_batteryinfo:file rw_file_perms;
 allow hal_usb_gadget_impl sysfs_extcon:dir search;
+
+# The gadget HAL reads back the configured function list; hal_usb_impl only ever had set_prop.
+get_prop(hal_usb_gadget_impl, vendor_usb_config_prop)
